/**
 * @defgroup SconGeo SconGeo — SVT/SSD Support Cone Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for the STAR silicon tracker support cone
 *        (SCON)
 *
 * @details
 * SconGeo (module name SCONGEO) models the mechanical support structure that
 * carries the STAR Silicon Vertex Tracker (SVT) and Silicon Strip Detector
 * (SSD) detector elements.  The support cone is a carbon-fibre/epoxy
 * composite structure located between the beam pipe and the inner field cage
 * of the TPC.  It was separated from the SVT geometry module and moved to the
 * CAVE level so that its material budget can be included independently of
 * whether the SVT electronics simulation is active.
 *
 * The module builds a rich set of sub-volumes:
 * - **SGRA**: the main graphite-epoxy cone body.
 * - **SCMY**: a mylar foil wrapped around the outside of the cone.
 * - **SBSP**: beam-pipe support assembly consisting of aluminium kinematic
 *   mounts (SAKM/SCKM), ceramic rollers (SBRL), stainless steel roller axes
 *   (SBRX), G10 support rings (SBSR/SBCR), and aluminium mounting blocks
 *   (SBMO, SBMI) on support rods (SMRD).
 * - **SROD**: carbon-composite support rods with a nomex-filled core (SRON),
 *   inner carbon shell (SROI), and central air hole (SROH).
 *
 * Four cone geometry versions (SVTG_conever 1–4) are available.  Versions 2,
 * 3, and 4 use progressively improved descriptions of the cable weight and
 * the SROD (carbon support rod) cross-section.
 *
 * ## Setup configurations
 *
 * | Setup name | onoff | conever | Description |
 * |------------|-------|---------|-------------|
 * | SCONof     | off   | —       | Support cone disabled |
 * | SCONon     | on    | default | Default support cone |
 * | SCON02     | off   | —       | Dummy (cone built by SVT geo) |
 * | SCON12     | on    | 2.0     | New cable weight estimate |
 * | SCON13     | on    | 3.0     | Updated cable weight |
 * | SCON14     | on    | 4.0     | Improved SROD description |
 *
 * ## Volume hierarchy
 * @code
 * SCON  (mother — placed in CAVE)
 * ├── SGRA          (graphite-epoxy cone body)
 * ├── SCMY          (mylar wrap)
 * ├── SBSP          (beam-pipe support assembly)
 * │   ├── SBMM      (mounting mother)
 * │   │   ├── SBMO  (outer mounting block)
 * │   │   ├── SBMI  (inner mounting block)
 * │   │   └── SMRD  (Al support rod)
 * │   ├── SAKM      (Al kinematic mount)
 * │   │   └── SCKM  (cutout)
 * │   ├── SBRL      (ceramic roller)
 * │   ├── SBRX      (stainless roller axis)
 * │   └── SBSR      (G10 support ring)
 * │       └── SBCR  (ring cutout)
 * └── SROD          (carbon composite rod)
 *     ├── SROH      (air hole)
 *     ├── SRON      (nomex core)
 *     └── SROI      (inner carbon shell)
 * @endcode
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @file SconGeo.xml
 * @brief SVT/SSD support cone geometry (SCONGEO module).
 * Carbon-fibre/epoxy cone with beam-pipe supports, kinematic mounts,
 * ceramic rollers, G10 rings, mylar wrap, and carbon composite rods.
 * Supports four cone versions (SVTG_conever 1–4).
 * Author: Victor Perev (31 October 2007).
 */

/**
 * @file SconConfig.xml
 * @brief Setup registry for the STAR SVT support cone (SCON).
 * Defines SCONof, SCONon, SCON02 (dummy), SCON12, SCON13, SCON14.
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
